#: ../manage_edit.rst:2
msgid "Manage and Edit"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:6
msgid "Managing Files and Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:8
msgid "User can tap on a folder to open it for browsing and on a file to preview it."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:10
msgid "Various operations can be performed in the menus, in the main list of files and folders, and in the preview itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:14
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:16
msgid "In the preview there is a 3-dot menu in the lower right corner that allows to perform some actions for the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:20
msgid "**Open** the file in other applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:22
msgid "**Download** a copy of the file to a folder on the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:24
msgid "**Rename** allows to rename the file if user have the permission to do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:26
msgid "**Delete** files from the folder if user have the permission."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:28
msgid "**Share** allows to send access information to people with an email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:30
msgid "**Share Via** let the user share the file with a third-party application. For example, by email or WhatsApp."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:32
msgid "**Get Public Link** gives user a link that anyone can use to access the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:34
msgid "**Share Manager** gives access to all the shares that exist for the file, where user can modify, delete, or add new shares."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:37
msgid "Download"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:39
msgid "A file can be downloaded using the **Download** option. Select Download from the context menu to download a file and select a folder from the phone storage of user's choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:47
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:49
msgid "A file can be deleted using the **Delete** option. Select it from the context menu to delete a file. Once the file is removed, it is no longer visible in the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:54
msgid "Rename"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:56
msgid "User can rename a file or folder using the **Rename** option. When pressing **Rename**, a field appears where user can enter the new name."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:61
msgid "Copy and Cut"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:63
msgid "The **Copy** option lets user copy a file and paste it into another folder of choice. The **Cut** option allows to remove a file from a certain folder and paste it into another."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:69
msgid "More Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:71
msgid "The **More Info** option allows to view the details of the file which are working on or viewing."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:79
msgid "Marking As Favorite"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:82
msgid "Adding to Favorite"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:84
msgid "User can add a file to the Favorites by pressing the **Star** icon. When adding a folder or a file to the Favorites, it will be marked with a green checkmark and will be accessible offline."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:90
msgid "Open Favorite Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:92
msgid "To open files from offline favorites, tap on the hamburger menu at the top left and select **Favorites**."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:96
msgid "In the **Offline Favorites** view, open a file by pressing the 3-dot button and selecting **Open File Locally**."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:100
msgid "After selecting the option, a list of applications that can open the file will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:105
msgid "Remove from Favorite"
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:107
msgid "To remove files from offline favorites, user can touch the yellow **Star** icon directly in the folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:111
msgid "Or press the hamburger menu at the top left and select **Favorites**."
msgstr ""

#: ../manage_edit.rst:115
msgid "In the **Offline Favorites** view, user can remove files by pressing the 3-dot button. Once the file is removed, it is no longer available offline."
msgstr ""
